---
layout: layouts/page.njk
title: Talent Acquisition
description: A higher-touch search practice for roles where volume hiring won't work — specialized, senior, or hard-to-fill positions.
glass: true
extraScripts:
  - /assets/js/count-up.js
  - /assets/js/faq-accordion.js
  - /assets/js/candidate-route.js
---
{% from "partials/icons.njk" import icon %}

{# ================================================================
   TALENT ACQUISITION — creative redesign
   (see claude_helper/TALENT-ACQUISITION-PAGE.md).

   The premium, retained-search employer service. Same IA as before:
     Hero → Difference → Included → Market map → Process → FAQ → CTA
   The recurring device is a MARKET, not a pipeline: partials/search-cluster.njk
   (candidate nodes with one found) plus a SEARCH TRACE
   (Discover → Map → Reach → Shortlist → Place) built from the shared
   candidate-route.njk. The hero and Difference sit on bg-surface so the page
   reads a shade richer than Recruitment & Staffing — strategic, not operational.

   Discipline unchanged: stats and the 6-month replacement guarantee stay
   confirmation-gated. See the TODOs.
   ================================================================ #}

{% set crumbs = [{ label: "Home", url: "/" }, { label: "Services", url: "/services/" }, { label: "Talent Acquisition" }] %}
{% set routeNodes = [
  { label: "Discover" }, { label: "Map" }, { label: "Reach" },
  { label: "Shortlist" }, { label: "Place" }
] %}

{# ---------- 1. Hero — 7/5 editorial split on bg-surface ----------
   Opens like a private search conversation. The search trace starts here,
   deliberately incomplete. ---------- #}
<section data-route-step="1" class="relative overflow-hidden bg-surface">
  <div class="section-container pb-14 pt-8 sm:pb-20 sm:pt-12">
    {% include "partials/breadcrumb.njk" %}

    <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-1 gap-y-12 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-12">
      <div class="lg:col-span-7 lg:pr-8">
        <p class="eyebrow">Confidential, retained search</p>

        <h1 class="mt-4 font-grotesk text-[2.75rem] font-bold leading-[1.02] tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-6xl lg:text-7xl">
          Precision hiring<br>for roles that matter.
        </h1>
        <p class="lead-copy mt-6 max-w-xl">
          A confidential, retained search practice for leadership and specialized
          roles — built to reach the candidate who was never going to apply, not
          just the one who did.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-8 flex flex-col gap-3 sm:flex-row">
          <a href="{{ '/contact/?role=employer' | url }}" class="btn-primary">
            {{ icon("arrow-right", "w-4 h-4") }} Start a search
          </a>
          <a href="{{ '/services/recruitment-staffing/' | url }}" class="btn-outline">
            Compare with staffing {{ icon("arrow-right", "w-4 h-4") }}
          </a>
        </div>

        {# The search trace, drawn at its first stage. #}
        {% set routeActive = 1 %}
        {% set routeProgress = true %}
        <div class="mt-12 max-w-lg">
          {% include "partials/candidate-route.njk" %}
        </div>

        {# TODO — confirm every figure with the client before launch (stats.json). #}
        <dl class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-x-12 gap-y-5 border-t border-ink/10 pt-6">
          {% for stat in stats.list.slice(0, 3) %}
          <div>
            <dd class="font-mono text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl"
                data-count-up data-target="{{ stat.value }}" data-suffix="{{ stat.suffix }}">0{{ stat.suffix }}</dd>
            <dt class="stat-label">{{ stat.label }}</dt>
          </div>
          {% endfor %}
        </dl>
      </div>

      <div class="lg:col-span-5">
        {% set coverImage = images.services["talent-acquisition"].cover %}
        <figure class="jp-frame">
          <span class="jp-frame-num" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
          <div class="jp-frame-media jp-reveal">
            <img src="{{ coverImage.url }}"
                 alt="{{ coverImage.alt }}"
                 width="1400" height="1750" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high"
                 class="aspect-[4/5] w-full object-cover">
          </div>

          {# The market motif, frosted so it reads over the photograph. #}
          <div class="ta-cluster-chip">
            <p class="meta">Search in progress</p>
            {% include "partials/search-cluster.njk" %}
          </div>

          <figcaption class="jp-frame-caption">Confidential search</figcaption>

          {# Frost — it floats over the photograph (THEME.md §3). #}
          <div class="glass-frost jp-fee">
            <p class="meta">Engagement</p>
            <p class="font-grotesk text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink">Retained</p>
          </div>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ---------- 2. The difference — two different problems ----------
   The most important block on the page. Same bg-surface tone as the hero so the
   two read as one opening statement. Opens with the assertion, then the ledger.
   ---------- #}
<section id="difference" data-route-step="2" class="scroll-mt-28 bg-surface py-16 sm:py-24">
  <div class="section-container">
    {% set comparison = [
      { k: "What it does", a: "Fills a defined role from an existing pool", b: "Builds a pipeline for a role that doesn't have one" },
      { k: "Timeline", a: "Days to weeks", b: "6–10 weeks" },
      { k: "Candidates", a: "Actively looking", b: "Usually not looking" },
      { k: "Best for", a: "Volume, contract, defined roles", b: "Leadership, specialized, competitive roles" },
      { k: "Terms", a: "Contingency", b: "Retained" }
    ] %}

    <div class="max-w-2xl">
      <h2 class="assertion sm:text-3xl">
        Staffing fills a role you have. Search finds the person who was never
        going to apply.
      </h2>
    </div>

    {# Two aligned panels: Talent Acquisition carries the weight — brand rule, faint
       tint, ink-weight values — so the premium side reads first. #}
    <div class="ta-compare mt-12">
      <dl class="ta-compare-col">
        <p class="ta-compare-h">Recruitment &amp; Staffing</p>
        {% for row in comparison %}
        <div class="ta-compare-item">
          <dt>{{ row.k }}</dt>
          <dd>{{ row.a }}</dd>
        </div>
        {% endfor %}
      </dl>
      <dl class="ta-compare-col ta-compare-col-strong">
        <p class="ta-compare-h">Talent Acquisition</p>
        {% for row in comparison %}
        <div class="ta-compare-item">
          <dt>{{ row.k }}</dt>
          <dd>{{ row.b }}</dd>
        </div>
        {% endfor %}
      </dl>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-6 meta leading-relaxed">
      Filling a defined role quickly?
      <a href="{{ '/services/recruitment-staffing/' | url }}" class="text-brand hover:underline">Recruitment &amp; Staffing</a>
      is the faster route.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

{# ---------- 3. What's included — a vertical search dossier ----------
   Sticky heading on lg; the four capabilities scroll past and the reader's
   current one takes the route node. ---------- #}
<section id="included" data-route-step="3" class="section-container scroll-mt-28 py-16 sm:py-24">
  {% set included = [
    { icon: "target", t: "Executive & specialized search", d: "Dedicated, retained search for leadership and niche technical roles — not a contingency posting run in parallel by three other firms." },
    { icon: "users", t: "Passive candidate sourcing", d: "Direct, confidential outreach to people who aren't job-searching — where the strongest candidates for a senior role usually are." },
    { icon: "chart", t: "Market mapping", d: "A clear view of where the right candidates sit today, and what it takes to reach them." },
    { icon: "support", t: "Long-term partnership model", d: "A dedicated search partner who knows the role and the team, not a transactional vendor relationship." }
  ] %}

  <div class="grid gap-y-10 lg:grid-cols-[17rem_1fr] lg:gap-x-16">
    <div class="lg:sticky lg:top-28 lg:self-start">
      <h2 class="section-title">What a retained search includes.</h2>
      <p class="lead-copy mt-4">
        A higher-touch practice for roles where a job posting was never going to
        be enough.
      </p>
    </div>

    <ol class="jp-index" data-jp-index>
      {% for item in included %}
      <li class="jp-index-row" data-jp-item>
        <div class="jp-index-head">
          <span class="jp-index-num">0{{ loop.index }}</span>
          <span class="jp-index-node" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="jp-index-icon">{{ icon(item.icon, "w-4 h-4") }}</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="card-title mt-3">{{ item.t }}</h3>
        <p class="body-copy mt-1.5">{{ item.d }}</p>
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

{# ---------- 4. Market mapping — the signature section ----------
   The clearest distinction from ordinary staffing: a zig-zag on a paper band,
   the candidate-map motif overlaid on the photograph. ---------- #}
<section id="map" data-route-step="4" class="scroll-mt-28 border-y border-white/60 bg-paper/50 py-16 sm:py-24">
  <div class="section-container">
    <div class="max-w-2xl">
      <h2 class="section-title">What a market map gives you.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 grid grid-cols-1 gap-10 sm:grid-cols-5 sm:items-center sm:gap-12">
      <div class="sm:col-span-3">
        <p class="body-copy text-[17px]">
          Who's doing this job today and where, what they're paid, which
          companies are the realistic feeder pool, and how long a move from
          each typically takes.
        </p>
        <p class="highlight mt-7">You keep it whether or not you hire through us.</p>
      </div>

      {% set plate = images.services["talent-acquisition"].plate %}
      <figure class="ta-map-frame sm:col-span-2">
        <img src="{{ plate.url }}" alt="{{ plate.alt }}"
             width="{{ plate.width }}" height="{{ plate.height }}" loading="lazy"
             class="aspect-[4/3] w-full object-cover">
        <div class="ta-map-overlay">{% include "partials/search-cluster.njk" %}</div>
        <figcaption class="meta px-4 pb-4 pt-3">{{ plate.caption }}</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ---------- 5. The process — a search trace ----------
   Ordinal; the stage the reader is level with is current, earlier stages read as
   assembled. Vertical trace on mobile. No durations (source keeps this page
   without them). ---------- #}
<section id="procedure" data-route-step="5" class="section-container scroll-mt-28 py-16 sm:py-24">
  {% set steps = [
    { label: "Discovery", description: "Understand the role, the team, and what success looks like a year in." },
    { label: "Market mapping", description: "Identify where qualified candidates actually are." },
    { label: "Outreach", description: "Direct, confidential approach to passive candidates." },
    { label: "Shortlist", description: "A small, vetted slate — not a wide net." },
    { label: "Placement", description: "Offer support and a 6-month replacement guarantee." }
  ] %}
  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <p class="eyebrow">Step by step</p>
    <h2 class="section-title mt-2">A search built around the role.</h2>
  </div>

  <ol class="jp-journey mt-14" data-jp-journey>
    {% for step in steps %}
    <li class="jp-journey-step{% if loop.first %} is-current{% endif %}" data-jp-node>
      <span class="jp-journey-num">0{{ loop.index }}</span>
      <span class="jp-journey-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <p class="jp-journey-label">{{ step.label }}</p>
      <p class="jp-journey-desc">{{ step.description }}</p>
    </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ol>
</section>

{# ---------- 6. FAQ — a confidential search docket ---------- #}
{% set faqKey = "talent-acquisition" %}
{% set faqTitle = "Before you commission a search." %}
{% include "partials/faq-route.njk" %}

{# ---------- 7. Closing CTA ---------- #}
{% set ctaStamp = "Ready when you are" %}
{% set ctaHeadline = "Have a role that's hard to fill?" %}
{% set ctaSubtext = "Let's talk about what a dedicated search would look like." %}
{% set ctaLabel = "Start a Conversation" %}
{% set ctaHref = "/contact/?role=employer" %}
{% include "partials/cta-section.njk" %}
